invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_table.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: one limb of one entry of the table of multiples of G is off by
  one: the X coordinate of 3 * 16^17 * G. The base multiplication reads
  it for one digit of one window, so a random scalar is wrong one time in
  sixteen and no fixed vector need notice. bin/p256_equiv_test recomputes
  every entry from G with p256_point_add and p256_point_affine and
  compares each coordinate byte for byte.

--- old
        {{{UINT64_C(0x3a63c39731815e69), UINT64_C(0x6df9cbd6dcdd2802),
--- new
        {{{UINT64_C(0x3a63c39731815e6a), UINT64_C(0x6df9cbd6dcdd2802),
